build: 2026-06-28 v10.76.43 (Dropdown stable from the start — stop re-seed rebuilds)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.42. Fixes "Genre/Tonart dropdown ist am Anfang noch nicht stabil".
  After the 10.76.41 fix the menus were fine in steady state, but a freshly-opened dropdown
  could still snap shut in the first seconds of a take. Cause: every time the music
  re-seeds (once at start, then periodically), it updated two screen-level values — the
  live AI caption text and a "has anything been composed" note count — and changing those
  rebuilt the WHOLE main screen, which closes any open dropdown (the panels are type-erased,
  so a rebuild loses the menu). Fix: the caption now lives in its own tiny view that
  refreshes alone, and the note-count gate became a one-time on/off flag instead of a value
  that changes every re-seed. So re-seeding no longer rebuilds the screen → the dropdowns
  stay open and selectable from the very first moment. build-error-resolver: GO.
  Test: 10.76.43 → tap Create from Within, immediately open Compose ▸ Composition ▸ Genre
  / Tonart — it should stay open and let you pick, even right at the start while the first
  notes are generating. Still launches straight to Studio.
